## Derivative work

ScreenMine is a port of **CoScreen** (1.21.4 → Minecraft 26.3). CoScreen was
authored by **Ma3stro567** and was distributed under the AGPL-3.0. Substantial
parts of its source code — including `BrowserInstance`, `PlaybackSync`,
`AppState`, `StreamInfo`, `Packets`, `NetClient`, `Cfg`, `Settings`, `Lang`,
`ScreenWorld` and `PlacedScreen` — were carried over into this project and
modified.

Under AGPL-3.0 §5(a), this work is therefore distributed under the same licence,
and §4 requires that the copyright and licence notices above be preserved. The
original CoScreen copyright notice is retained here.

Note: CoScreen's own `LICENSE` file contains only the unmodified FSF boilerplate
and names no copyright holder, so the attribution above is taken from the
`authors` field of its `fabric.mod.json`.

## Changes made

The port replaces, among other things:

- Yarn mappings with Mojang names (Minecraft 26.1+ ships unobfuscated)
- GLFW with SDL3
- the `RenderSystem` render-state API with `RenderPipeline` / `RenderPipeline`
  world-space submission via `com.mojang.renderpearl`
- CinemaMod MCEF (dead at 1.21.4) with `mcef-modern`
- the mod, package and asset identities: CoScreen → ScreenMine

## -only vs -or-later

CoScreen does not say. There is no `license` field in its `fabric.mod.json`, no
licence headers in its sources, and no grant statement anywhere. Its `LICENSE`
file is the unmodified FSF boilerplate; the word "only" appears there only
incidentally in the body of the AGPL text and carries no grant meaning.

Because the grant is silent, `AGPL-3.0 section 14` applies: whoever receives the
work may choose any published version of the licence. So the absence of a
statement is **not** the same as an `-only` grant, and does not resolve to one.

ScreenMine is therefore released as **`AGPL-3.0-only`** -- a conservative choice
made by ScreenMine's author, not an interpretation of what CoScreen intended.

To settle it, the question has to go to **Ma3stro567**, who holds the copyright
to CoScreen. They are the only party who can state the intended grant, and the
only one who can permit re-licensing ScreenMine under different terms. An issue
asking the question should be opened on the CoScreen repository; the answer will
be recorded here.

